"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkdocs=globalThis.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[2266],{7829(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"welcome","metadata":{"permalink":"/SoCMake/pr-preview/pr-235/blog/welcome","source":"@site/blog/2026-06-15-welcome.md","title":"Welcome to the SoCMake Blog","description":"Welcome to the official SoCMake blog! This is where we will post release notes, feature highlights, tutorials, and news from the project.","date":"2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"socmake","permalink":"/SoCMake/pr-preview/pr-235/blog/tags/socmake"},{"inline":true,"label":"announcement","permalink":"/SoCMake/pr-preview/pr-235/blog/tags/announcement"}],"readingTime":1.62,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"SoCMake Team","title":"HEP-SoC","url":"https://github.com/HEP-SoC","socials":{},"key":null,"page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"welcome","title":"Welcome to the SoCMake Blog","authors":[{"name":"SoCMake Team","title":"HEP-SoC","url":"https://github.com/HEP-SoC"}],"image":"/img/SoCMakeLogo3.svg","tags":["socmake","announcement"]},"unlisted":false},"content":"Welcome to the official SoCMake blog! This is where we will post release notes, feature highlights, tutorials, and news from the project.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What is SoCMake?\\n\\n**SoCMake** is a hardware build system built on top of CMake. It extends the mature CMake ecosystem to cover the specific needs of hardware and SoC design \u2014 RTL simulation, code generation, FPGA implementation, and synthesis \u2014 without reinventing the wheel.\\n\\nThe core idea is simple: instead of learning yet another domain-specific build tool, designers can use the same CMake workflow used in many software projects, and SoCMake handles the rest.\\n\\n## Key Features\\n\\n- **First-class C/C++ support** \u2014 ideal for SystemC testbenches and mixed HW/SW projects\\n- **Cross-compilation** \u2014 compile target CPU application code for ARM, RISC-V and other architectures alongside your RTL\\n- **Extensive simulation support** \u2014 Verilator, Icarus Verilog, GHDL, Xcelium, VCS, Questasim, Vivado Simulator, and cocotb\\n- **RTL toolchain integration** \u2014 linting (Verible, vhdl_linter), conversion (sv2v), synthesis (Yosys, Vivado), and register description (PeakRDL, desyrdl)\\n- **IP block package management** \u2014 package IPs as self-contained repositories and manage dependencies via [CPM.cmake](https://github.com/cpm-cmake/CPM.cmake)\\n\\n## Supported Languages and Tools\\n\\n| Category | Tools |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Languages** | C, C++, SystemC, ASM, Verilog, SystemVerilog, VHDL, SystemRDL, IP-XACT |\\n| **Simulation** | Verilator, Icarus Verilog, GHDL, Xcelium, VCS, Questasim, Vivado Sim, cocotb |\\n| **Linting** | Verible, vhdl_linter |\\n| **Conversion** | sv2v |\\n| **Synthesis** | Yosys, Vivado |\\n| **Register tools** | PeakRDL (regblock, halcpp, html, socgen), desyrdl |\\n\\n## Getting Started\\n\\nSoCMake has minimal dependencies \u2014 only CMake \u2265 3.27 and `make` or `ninja`. The quickest way to try it is via the one-time bootstrap:\\n\\n```bash\\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HEP-SoC/SoCMake/develop/bootstrap/bootstrap.sh | sh\\n```\\n\\nThen create a `CMakeLists.txt`:\\n\\n```cmake\\ncmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.27)\\nproject(my_soc NONE)\\n\\nfind_package(socmake REQUIRED)\\n\\nadd_ip(my_ip)\\nip_sources(my_ip SYSTEMVERILOG src/my_module.sv)\\n```\\n\\nSee the [Getting Started](../docs/getting_started) guide and the [Examples](../docs/category/examples) for full walkthroughs.\\n\\n## About This Blog\\n\\nWe will use this space to announce new releases, explain design decisions, and share tips for getting the most out of SoCMake. Stay tuned!"}]}}')}}]);